From 63203ddc0f7225e6aae8c64847e101d4b7af0b99 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nicholasbulka <nicholasbulka@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 30 Apr 2026 07:31:50 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] v4.27 wasm32 patches for MT=ON browser/Node-worker target
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Real elaboration runs (#eval x for `def x : Nat := 42` returns "42") in a
WASM build hosted by Node worker_threads, demonstrating the path to a
static-files-only browser IDE without server-side compilation.

Categories of patches:
- Build config (CMakeLists.txt, lakefile.toml.in): MT-aware
  EMSCRIPTEN_SETTINGS so the wasm-feature flags (-pthread, -matomics,
  -mbulk-memory) are dropped when MULTI_THREAD=OFF and propagated to
  Lake's .c.o.export builds when ON.
- 8 wasm-ld signature mismatches (memory.cpp, interrupt.cpp, io.cpp,
  module.cpp x2, compact.cpp, ir_interpreter.cpp, uv/dns.cpp,
  uv/event_loop.cpp, uv/system.cpp) — Lean's codegen ABI and the C
  externs disagreed on argc; WASM strict signature checking exposed it.
- libuv stubs (uv/tcp.cpp, uv/udp.cpp): the v4.27 Emscripten ifdef
  branch declared but didn't define several entry points; without
  stubs wasm-ld emitted `unreachable` for each.
- MT=OFF runtime safety nets (object.cpp, thread.h): defensive null
  guards on g_task_manager and a missing adopt_lock_t/release() in the
  MT=OFF unique_lock stub. Not on the MT=ON path but lets the build
  system survive single-threaded compile attempts.

Authoritative inventory and rationale per file in the host repo at
docs (memory/v427_patch_inventory.md). Verify with
`git -C vendor/lean4-src diff --stat` — should report 15 files, ~243/-29.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
